%% Anything not drawn here is forbidden.
%% One state, and no arrow out of it: audit.records is append-only three ways
%% (revoked grants, no update or delete policy under FORCE, a trigger), so a
%% record that exists is the record that was written. This feature reads that
%% state and moves nothing; every transition below is already built.
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  state "audit.records" as RecordMachine {
    state "written" as a_written

    [*] --> a_written : recordWithin, inside the acting module's transaction / built
    a_written --> [*]
  }

  note right of a_written
    Terminal on arrival. A correction to what a record says is a
    second record, never a change to the first (blueprint 7.4).
    The reason, when the action requires one, is on the record
    itself; the record and the action it describes commit together.
  end note
